{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2006-10002","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"XML::Parser versions through 2.45 for Perl could overflow the pre-allocated buffer size cause a heap corruption (double free or corruption) and crashes.\n\nA :utf8 PerlIO layer, parse_stream() in Expat.xs could overflow…","description":"XML::Parser versions through 2.45 for Perl could overflow the pre-allocated buffer size cause a heap corruption (double free or corruption) and crashes.\n\nA :utf8 PerlIO layer, parse_stream() in Expat.xs could overflow the XML input buffer because Perl's read() returns decoded characters while SvPV() gives back multi-byte UTF-8 bytes that can exceed the pre-allocated buffer size. This can cause heap corruption (double free or corruption) and crashes.","published":"2026-03-19T11:03:46.888Z","lastModified":"2026-04-29T14:36:41.837Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"CRITICAL","cvss":9.8},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":{"vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":9.8,"baseSeverity":"CRITICAL","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"},"v4_0":null},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-122","name":"CWE-122 Heap-based Buffer Overflow","source":"cve.org"},{"cweId":"CWE-176","name":"CWE-176 Improper Handling of Unicode Encoding","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"TODDR","product":"XML::Parser","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"2.45"}],"platforms":[]}],"configurations":[],"references":[{"url":"https://rt.cpan.org/Ticket/Display.html?id=19859","source":"cve.org","tags":["issue-tracking"]},{"url":"https://github.com/cpan-authors/XML-Parser/issues/64","source":"cve.org","tags":["issue-tracking"]},{"url":"https://metacpan.org/release/TODDR/XML-Parser-2.46/changes","source":"cve.org","tags":["release-notes"]},{"url":"https://github.com/cpan-authors/XML-Parser/commit/56b0509dfc6b559cd7555ea81ee62e3622069255.patch","source":"cve.org","tags":["patch"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/03/19/1","source":"cve.org","tags":[]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/03/22/3","source":"cve.org","tags":[]}],"exploit":null,"credits":[],"sources":["cve.org"],"primarySource":"cve.org"}
{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2006-10003","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"XML::Parser versions through 2.47 for Perl has an off-by-one heap buffer overflow in st_serial_stack.\n\nIn the case (stackptr == stacksize - 1), the stack will NOT be expanded. Then the new value will be written at loc…","description":"XML::Parser versions through 2.47 for Perl has an off-by-one heap buffer overflow in st_serial_stack.\n\nIn the case (stackptr == stacksize - 1), the stack will NOT be expanded. Then the new value will be written at location (++stackptr), which equals stacksize and therefore falls just outside the allocated buffer.\n\nThe bug can be observed when parsing an XML file with very deep element nesting","published":"2026-03-19T11:08:04.341Z","lastModified":"2026-07-15T01:28:08.168Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"CRITICAL","cvss":9.8},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":{"vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":9.8,"baseSeverity":"CRITICAL","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"},"v4_0":null},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-193","name":"CWE-193 Off-by-one Error","source":"cve.org"},{"cweId":"CWE-122","name":"CWE-122 Heap-based Buffer Overflow","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"TODDR","product":"XML::Parser","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":null,"versionEndIncluding":"2.47"}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10.1","versions":[{"version":"0:2.47-6.1.el10_1","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":"*","versionEndIncluding":null}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 Extended Update Support","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux_eus:10.0","versions":[{"version":"0:2.47-6.el10_0.1","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":"*","versionEndIncluding":null}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 Extende